[2026-05-31T14:52:52.039502] [INFO] Node Code Reviewer - Event EventType.TOOL_CALL - Tool call read_file_segment for node Code Reviewer Details: {'tool_result': {'path': 'csv_handler.py', 'encoding': 'utf-8-sig', 'newline': '\n', 'start_line': 1, 'end_line': 31, 'line_count': 40, 'lines_returned': 31, 'total_lines': 31, 'snippet': '"""\nThis module handles CSV file operations for saving query results.\n"""\n\nimport os\nimport pandas as pd  # Ensure pandas is imported\n\nclass CSVHandler:\n    def save_to_csv(self, data, filename):\n        # Validate the filename\n        if not isinstance(filename, str) or not filename.endswith(\'.csv\'):\n            print(f"Error: \'{filename}\' is not a valid filename. It must end with .csv.")\n            return\n\n        # Validate the data\n        if not data or not isinstance(data, (list, dict)):\n            print("Error: No data provided or data is not in a valid format.")\n            return\n\n        if os.path.exists(filename):\n            overwrite = input(f"The file {filename} already exists. Do you want to overwrite it? (yes/no): ").lower()\n            if overwrite != \'yes\':\n                print("File not saved.")\n                return\n\n        try:\n            df = pd.DataFrame(data)\n            df.to_csv(filename, index=False)  # Writes DataFrame to CSV.\n            print(f"Data successfully saved to {filename}.")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"Error occurred while saving to CSV: {e}")\n', 'truncated': False, 'file_size': 1130, 'modified_ts': 1780231923.3119287, 'mode': 'line_range'}, 'tool_name': 'read_file_segment', 'success': True, 'result_size': 1438, 'arguments': {'path': 'csv_handler.py', 'line_count': 40}, 'stage': 'after'} Duration: 0.0019843578338623047
