[2026-05-31T14:54:05.014372] [INFO] Node Chief Product Officer - Event EventType.TOOL_CALL - Tool call save_file for node Chief Product Officer Details: {'tool_result': None, 'tool_name': 'save_file', 'success': None, 'result_size': 0, 'arguments': {'path': 'docs/manual.md', 'content': "# ArXiv Query Tool User Manual\n\n## Introduction\nThe ArXiv Query Tool is designed to streamline the research process by allowing users to query the ArXiv database efficiently. It provides flexible and time-sensitive search capabilities, enabling researchers to find relevant papers quickly. Users can choose to print query results to the console or save them to a specified CSV file for later use.\n\n## Main Functions\n1. **Search ArXiv Database**: Perform a search on the ArXiv database using various query parameters such as title, author, and keywords.\n2. **Print Results**: Display the search results directly in the console for immediate review.\n3. **Save to CSV**: Save the search results to a CSV file for easy sharing and offline analysis.\n\n## Installation\nTo set up the environment for the ArXiv Query Tool, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Clone the Repository**:  Clone the repository from the version control system to your local machine.\n   ```bash\n   git clone <repository_url>\n   cd <repository_directory>\n   ```\n\n2. **Initialize Python Environment**: Set up the Python environment by running the following command:\n   ```bash\n   uv lock\n   uv venv\n   ```\n\n3. **Install Dependencies**: Install the required Python packages by executing:\n   ```bash\n   uv add <package_list>\n   ```\n   Make sure to replace `<package_list>` with the actual list of packages needed for the project.\n\n## Usage\nTo use the ArXiv Query Tool, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Run the Tool**: Execute the main script to start the tool. You can run it using:\n   ```bash\n   uv run <script_name>\n   ```\n   Replace `<script_name>` with the name of the script that initializes the tool.\n\n2. **Input Query Parameters**: When prompted, enter the necessary parameters for your search query, including:\n   - Title\n   - Author\n   - Keywords\n\n3. **Choose Output Option**: After executing the search, you will be presented with an option to either:\n   - Print results to console\n   - Save results to a CSV file\n   \n4. **View Results**: Based on your selection, either view the results in the console or find the generated CSV file in your specified directory.\n\n## Conclusion\nThe ArXiv Query Tool is a powerful resource for researchers looking to enhance their workflow and access relevant academic papers efficiently. For any issues or contributions, please refer to the project's issue tracker or contact the maintainers.\n", 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'mode': 'overwrite'}, 'stage': 'before'} 
