cript to start the tool. You can run it using:\\n   ```bash\\n   uv run <script_name>\\n   ```\\n   Replace `<script_name>` with the name of the script that initializes the tool.\\n\\n2. **Input Query Parameters**: When prompted, enter the necessary parameters for your search query, including:\\n   - Title\\n   - Author\\n   - Keywords\\n\\n3. **Choose Output Option**: After executing the search, you will be presented with an option to either:\\n   - Print results to console\\n   - Save results to a CSV file\\n   \\n4. **View Results**: Based on your selection, either view the results in the console or find the generated CSV file in your specified directory.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\nThe ArXiv Query Tool is a powerful resource for researchers looking to enhance their workflow and access relevant academic papers efficiently. For any issues or contributions, please refer to the project\'s issue tracker or contact the maintainers.\\n","encoding":"utf-8","mode":"overwrite"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'content': '{\n  "path": "docs/manual.md",\n  "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\ArXiv_digest_20260531144726\\\\code_workspace\\\\docs\\\\manual.md",\n  "size": 2382\n}', 'tool_call_id': 'call_6z3tqH5d6g4gCAoFsbKW896r', 'metadata': {'tool_name': 'save_file', 'source': 'Chief Product Officer'}}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'The user manual has been successfully created and saved as `manual.md` in the `docs` folder. It includes an introduction to the ArXiv Query Tool, its main functions, installation instructions, and usage guidelines. You can now review or distribute this manual as needed. If you require any further modifications or additional content, please let me know!'}], 'metadata': {'source': 'Chief Product Officer'}}], 'context_trace_complete': True}}], 'node_type': 'agent', 'input_count': 3, 'predecessors': ['Manual Phase Prompt for User', 'USER', 'Chief Product Officer'], 'successors': ['Manua